00:30:11.930 --> 00:30:14.660
But we'll still get a
little bit spooked by that.

00:30:14.660 --> 00:30:15.640
We'll react.

00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:17.580
We'll say, "We're going to Mars."

00:30:17.580 --> 00:30:20.820
Oh, NASA doesn't have
a spaceship to do so.

00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:23.370
We have one that kinda works but...

00:30:23.370 --> 00:30:24.750
Does anyone else have a spaceship?

00:30:24.750 --> 00:30:26.057
And Elon raises his hand.

00:30:26.057 --> 00:30:28.560
"I've got one right
here in the warehouse."

00:30:28.560 --> 00:30:29.790
So, then.

00:30:29.790 --> 00:30:31.971
- Right here next to the
pool and the tennis court.

00:30:31.971 --> 00:30:36.150
- So we end up using an Elon spaceship

00:30:36.150 --> 00:30:38.670
that he diligently built,

00:30:38.670 --> 00:30:40.550
researched, designed, and built,

00:30:40.550 --> 00:30:41.383
and that's good,

00:30:41.383 --> 00:30:43.460
but that's not Elon landing on Mars.

00:30:43.460 --> 00:30:45.580
That's the American tax
payer landing on Mars.

00:30:45.580 --> 00:30:47.025
That's the difference.

00:30:47.025 --> 00:30:48.030
- So it's no longer privatized.

00:30:48.030 --> 00:30:50.370
- It's not a business model
'cause we're doing it.

00:30:50.370 --> 00:30:51.540
- Yeah.

00:30:51.540 --> 00:30:52.640
- There it is.

00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:53.473
